	(text "GPIO10 drives the tip divider only; pulse for settled conversions.\nAIN0 = tip, AIN1 = half excitation, AIN2 = pack NTC via R88 from the BQ24074 TS node, AIN3 = GND.\nTip: R = 10 kΩ × AIN0 / (2 × AIN1 − AIN0) with bracketing reference reads.\nPack: the TS node carries the pack internal NTC (10 k, B 3435 typ.) biased by the charger (INTC 72..78 µA while charging) plus R42 470 k to 3V3.\nR_NTC = AIN2 / (I_TS + (3V3 − AIN2) / 470 k), I_TS = 75 µA while charging (dock present), else 0; AIN2 < ~0.28 V means no charger bias. Use the ±256 mV range off dock.\nHardware charge limits stay on the BQ24074 TS pin (0.3 V hot / 2.1 V cold); R42 shifts the hot trip by about +2 °C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
